# What the build context carries. Not a copy of .gitignore, and the difference is the
# point: `models/` is gitignored and must be *in* the context, because the image ships
# the artifacts; `reports/` is tracked and must be out, because the service never reads
# a figure.
#
# data/ alone is hundreds of megabytes. Sending it would be paid on every build.
data/
mlruns/
reports/
notebooks/
docs/
tests/

.git/
.github/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

.env
.DS_Store
Makefile
